    "nextNodeId": 89,
    "nodes": {
      "0": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": true
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "INPUT & OUTPUT\n\nIn this tutorial we'll teach you how to get user input and data into Wire.\n\nInputs are an essential part of creating a patch,\nWhen designing a patch, you are not only building a new effect or source.\nYou should also consider how the patch is controlled.\nDo you need sliders, toggles or menus? How do you name them? \nWhat ranges are used? Do you really need that many parameters?\nIt is up to you as a designer to answer these questions.\nIn this tutorial we'll give you the tools to do so."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 248.2823486328125,
          "width": 583.09765625,
          "x": -260.6693115234375,
          "y": -357.85858154296875
        },
        "class": {
          "id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
          "version": 1
        },
        "clock": "video",
        "color": "ffd0c117",
        "constants": {},
        "hidden": [
          "text",
          "alignment",
          "font-size",
          "fill"
        ],
        "name": "Comment",
        "thumbnail_visible": true
      },
      "1": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "INPUT\n\nInput nodes are a category of nodes that allow the user or host to interact with the patch.\nThe nodes from this category will determine the controls the user has in Arena/Avenue.\n\nThe  four nodes below are nodes that the user can interact with directly.\nFor example: The Color In node gives the user a color picker to work with.\n\nYou can interact with these nodes directly when they are on the canvas.\nBut this gets difficult as your patches grow in size.\nTo solve this we have a Dashboard panel on the right side of the interface.\n\nFrom here you can find, tweak, select, rearrange and rename your input nodes.\n\nIt is important to note that the order of parameters in the dashboard panel dictates the parameter order in Arena/Avenue. The naming is  also carried over.\n\nAssignment: Create an input node of choice, find it in the dashboard panel, rename it from the dashboard panel and move it to the top."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 686.6143798828125,
          "width": 758.56201171875,
          "x": -260.6693115234375,
          "y": -68.59864044189453
