      "6": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": false
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "TOGGLES\n\nSometimes sliders and menus are overkill for what you are trying to do: turning something on or off.\nThis is most commonly done with the Boolean type (true/false , 1/0).\nThe input version of this would be the Bool In.\nIt gives the user a box which they can turn on or off.\n\nIn the first example we've created a Bool In and renamed it to Bypass.\nThis is used to bypass the Colorize node.\n\nIn the second example, the patch is nearly the same.\nBut we are using the Not node to flip the output of the boolean (true = false, false = true).\nThis allows us to create an interface in which the effect is off by default and can be enabled on command."
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 909.0427856445312,
          "width": 820.2439575195312,
          "x": 1390.8885498046875,
